Part of #258 — Nostos Cloud.

Blocks live browser validation for #409 / PR #448.

## Context

Repository-side hosted onboarding is implemented and green in PR #448, but the external Clerk setup correctly stopped at `BLOCKED_NO_CLOUD_APP_ORIGIN`.

There is currently **no externally reachable Nostos Cloud compute deployment**:

- the release pipeline builds/pushes the production container;
- Neon Free, Backblaze B2, Clerk development and Paddle sandbox are already available for alpha;
- no app consumes the container;
- `app.nostos.page` is currently unused and available;
- `accounts.nostos.page` remains reserved for the preferred branded Clerk auth domain.

This issue is deliberately **not #435**.

#435 is the future paid-production migration (App Platform + managed PostgreSQL) and remains blocked by its documented revenue/reliability trigger. This issue owns only the smallest isolated alpha/staging compute origin needed to run and validate the already-built Cloud product.

## Goal

Make one real HTTPS Nostos Cloud staging/alpha application reachable at:

```text
https://app.nostos.page
```

using the existing single Nostos container/runtime and the existing alpha services.

Conceptually:

```text
app.nostos.page
      |
 HTTPS compute
      |
Nostos container :8080
DeploymentMode=Cloud
      |
      +-- Neon Free control plane/customer PostgreSQL
      +-- Backblaze B2 alpha storage
      +-- Clerk development instance
      +-- Paddle sandbox
      +-- managed AI/STT alpha credentials
```

Once this origin exists, #409 can finish the deterministic Clerk pass:

- OIDC application/client;
- `/signin-oidc` redirect;
- `/signout-callback-oidc`;
- audience/JWT smoke configuration;
- optional `accounts.nostos.page`;
- runtime client secret;
- real browser auth/onboarding smoke.

## Important boundary

Do **not** start the #435 production migration here.

Specifically, do not:

- migrate Neon to DigitalOcean Managed PostgreSQL;
- provision a production customer database cluster;
- move B2;
- perform production cutover/PITR work;
- promise production reliability;
- introduce a second Cloud frontend;
- change the current database-per-customer architecture.

Keep the existing €0/month alpha data/auth/billing providers intact.

## Hosting decision gate

A persistent external compute host may incur cost.

Before creating a paid resource, obtain Christian's explicit approval for the exact provider/tier/monthly cost.

The existing ADR's preferred compute platform is DigitalOcean App Platform, so a **compute-only staging/alpha service** there is the default persistent-host candidate if Christian approves the spend. Reuse Neon Free + B2 rather than pulling the rest of #435 forward.

A temporary tunnel/home-hosted endpoint may be used only for a short-lived OIDC smoke if Christian explicitly chooses that path. It is not the persistent Nostos Cloud alpha deployment.

Do not introduce a new hosting provider casually merely to find a free tier; any alternative should be justified against the existing hosting ADR.

## Runtime

Deploy the existing #401/#402 container/release artifact.

Requirements:

- same ASP.NET + Angular application;
- container port 8080;
- `Nostos__DeploymentMode=Cloud`;
- immutable image from the existing release/container pipeline where practical;
- no source build fork;
- no local durable customer data;
- all secrets injected through the host's secret/environment mechanism;
- health endpoints exposed;
- HTTPS required.

Do not commit runtime secrets.

## Environment configuration

Use the existing repo contracts and operator inventory.

At minimum, the Cloud app needs the existing environment-specific configuration/secrets for:

### Control plane / PostgreSQL

- `NOSTOS_CLOUD_CONTROL_PLANE_CONNECTION`
- `NOSTOS_CLOUD_POSTGRES_ADMIN_CONNECTION`
- `NOSTOS_CLOUD_POSTGRES_CUSTOMER_CONNECTION`

### Object storage

- `CloudObjectStorage__Bucket`
- `CloudObjectStorage__ServiceUrl`
- `CloudObjectStorage__Region`
- `NOSTOS_CLOUD_OBJECT_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY`
- `NOSTOS_CLOUD_OBJECT_STORAGE_SECRET_KEY`

### Authentication

Clerk values are intentionally incomplete until the origin exists.

After `https://app.nostos.page` is live, #409 owns the final Clerk pass and will provide:

- `CloudAuth__Authority`
- `CloudAuth__ClientId`
- `CloudAuth__Audience`
- `NOSTOS_CLOUD_AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET`

The deployment must therefore support a two-step bring-up if necessary:

1. create/bind the HTTPS host/origin without inventing Clerk values;
2. configure Clerk for the real origin;
3. inject the returned auth values and redeploy/restart;
4. run browser OIDC smoke.

Do not weaken Cloud authentication just to make the first deployment boot.

### Billing

Use Paddle sandbox only.

- `CloudBilling__Paddle__Environment=Sandbox`
- existing sandbox API/webhook runtime secrets

### Managed AI / STT

Use the current alpha managed-provider secret names from current main/operator docs.
Do not reintroduce old Gemini direct-provider configuration if main has migrated managed LLM transport.

### Data protection

Use the existing Cloud data-protection key contract from #401/#402.

## DNS

Bind:

```text
app.nostos.page -> chosen Cloud staging/alpha host
```

The `nostos.page` DNS zone remains managed by Vercel.

Do not repurpose:

- `nostos.page` (marketing)
- `docs.nostos.page` (docs)
- `accounts.nostos.page` (reserved for Clerk hosted-auth custom domain)

## GitHub staging environment

After the app is externally reachable, configure the existing GitHub `staging` environment according to #402:

- `NOSTOS_STAGING_BASE_URL=https://app.nostos.page`
- keep `NOSTOS_STAGING_MANAGED_AI_SMOKE` false until explicitly enabling the bounded live AI smoke;
- add only the staging-specific auth smoke secret/token if/when #409's Clerk configuration provides it.

Do not store general provider/runtime secrets in repository files.

## Validation before handing back to #409

Verify:

- `https://app.nostos.page` resolves correctly;
- HTTPS certificate is valid;
- production container is actually running in Cloud mode;
- `/health/live` succeeds;
- `/health/ready` succeeds once required external services are configured;
- `/api/runtime/capabilities` reports Cloud;
- anonymous Cloud session/auth boundary behaves as expected;
- no secret values are exposed in logs/client responses;
- SelfHosted behavior remains untouched;
- the deployment can be restarted without losing customer state.

Then return to #409 with the exact real origin:

```text
CLOUD_ORIGIN=https://app.nostos.page
```

so Clerk can be configured deterministically.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] explicit hosting/tier/cost decision is recorded before any paid resource is created;
- [ ] one isolated alpha/staging Cloud compute deployment exists;
- [ ] `app.nostos.page` points to it over valid HTTPS;
- [ ] existing Neon Free/B2/Clerk dev/Paddle sandbox architecture is preserved;
- [ ] Nostos runs in `DeploymentMode=Cloud`;
- [ ] health/capability checks pass;
- [ ] GitHub staging base URL is configured after the host is live;
- [ ] no production migration work from #435 is pulled forward;
- [ ] #409 is unblocked for final Clerk configuration and live OIDC/onboarding smoke.

## Non-goals

- production launch;
- paid PostgreSQL migration;
- #408 security/privacy/account-deletion hardening;
- direct-media delivery optimization;
- changing public pricing;
- redesigning CI/CD;
- changing the marketing site beyond the later focused CTA handoff.

# LIVE-OPS-01 — Production-stable daily-use slice

## Цел
Крум иска да започне да използва BEG_Work **още докато продължава разработката**. Първият реално използваем пакет трябва да е:

1. **Заявки**
2. **Склад**
3. **Машини / инструменти / активи**
4. Връзките между трите

Това НЕ отменя текущия Wave 0 roadmap и НЕ разрешава merge/deploy автоматично.

## Задължителна схема за работа
GPT = продуктов/UX координатор и финален синтез.
CODEX = независим технически одит, архитектура, тестове, production-readiness критерии.
CLAUDE = независим code/UX audit и предложение за минимален стабилен implementation slice.

Преди код:
- CODEX и CLAUDE да прегледат съществуващия код и данни;
- да установят кое работи реално, кое е частично и кое липсва;
- да се съгласува един общ минимален функционален договор;
- GPT да изготвя визуални frontend mockup-и;
- Крум да одобри UX потока и mockup-а;
- чак след това се подготвя implementation task.

## Съществуваща основа за одит
Backend:
- `backend/app/models/warehouse.py`
- `backend/app/routes/warehouses.py`
- `backend/app/routes/warehouse_batches.py`
- `backend/app/routes/material_smr.py`
- `backend/app/routes/materials_baseline.py`
- `backend/app/routes/assets_items.py`
- `backend/app/routes/assets_units.py`
- `backend/app/routes/assets_custody.py`
- `backend/app/routes/assets_repairs.py`
- `backend/app/routes/assets_qr.py`

Frontend:
- `frontend/src/pages/WarehousesPage.js`
- `frontend/src/pages/InventoryDashboardPage.js`
- `frontend/src/pages/AssetsUnitsPage.js`
- `frontend/src/pages/AssetUnitDetailPage.js`
- `frontend/src/pages/MyToolsPage.js`
- `frontend/src/components/ProjectMaterialLedger.js`
- `frontend/src/components/warehouse/*`

Existing tests:
- `backend/tests/test_warehouse_material_ledger.py`
- `backend/tests/test_inventory_dashboard.py`
- `backend/tests/test_material_smr_flow.py`
- `backend/tests/test_materials_baseline.py`

## Минимален бизнес поток за съгласуване

### Заявки
`Заявено → Одобрено → Подготвя се → Изписано → В транспорт → Получено`

Всяка заявка трябва да има:
- обект;
- заявител;
- материал/машина;
- количество;
- мерна единица;
- нужда до дата;
- склад/източник;
- статус;
- кой е одобрил;
- кой е изписал;
- кой е получил;
- история/AuditEvent.

### Склад
За всеки материал:
- физическа наличност;
- резервирано;
- свободно;
- изписано;
- очаквана доставка;
- движения;
- склад;
- обект;
- партида/цена когато е приложимо.

### Машини / инструменти
Ясен operational indicator:
- 🟢 В склад
- 🟡 На обект
- 🔵 При човек
- 🟠 За ремонт
- 🔴 Просрочена / липсва
- ⚫ Бракувана

За всяка машина:
- asset/QR;
- текущо местоположение;
- текущ отговорник;
- обект;
- дата на предаване;
- очаквано връщане;
- история на движенията;
- ремонт/дефект;
- снимка, ако съществува.

## UX принцип
Phone-first за оперативните действия, desktop-first за контролния екран.

Начален desktop control screen:
- горе: KPI карти за заявки, складови дефицити, просрочени машини;
- ляво: навигация Заявки / Склад / Машини;
- център: активни заявки и критични отклонения;
- дясно: бързи действия и машинни индикатори;
- без излишни несвързани модули.

## Definition of READY FOR IMPLEMENTATION
CODEX + CLAUDE трябва независимо да потвърдят:
1. точния съществуващ data model и routes;
2. кои части могат да се използват без migration risk;
3. липсващите връзки Request → Reservation → Warehouse Movement → Receipt;
4. липсващите връзки Asset → Custody → Project/Person → Return/Repair;
5. required tests;
6. rollback boundary;
7. дали може да се пусне като isolated stable slice без да блокира Wave 0;
8. конфликтите с canonical FLOW/Wave решенията.

## Hard boundaries
- Няма merge/deploy/production activation без отделно решение на Крум.
- Няма production DB migration преди dry-run + backup + rollback proof.
- Не се променят канонични FLOW правила без решение на Крум.
- Mockup approval НЕ е code approval.
- Първо audit + UX agreement, после implementation.

## Standing authorization for agent collaboration
Крум разрешава CODEX и CLAUDE да използват наличните им PC/Computer Use способности за директно предаване на analysis, corrections и HANDOFF-и помежду си в рамките на LIVE-OPS-01. Ако платформата технически изисква action-time confirmation, това не може да се заобикаля; записва се blocker-ът честно.
